# EduFlex 🎓

EduFlex is a full-stack web application designed to simplify and streamline educational management tasks. It features a modern React-based frontend and a powerful Node.js/Express backend with RESTful APIs.

---

## 🔧 Project Structure
EduFlex/
├── frontend/ # React.js client-side app
├── backend/ # Node.js/Express server-side app
└── README.md # Project documentation

---

## 🚀 Features
- 🧑‍🏫 Role-based access for Students, Teachers, Admins
- 📚 Course management
- 📝 Assignments and submissions
- 📊 Real-time analytics and dashboards
- 🔐 Authentication and Authorization (JWT)
- 📬 Email notifications

---

## ⚙️ Technologies Used

### Frontend (React)
- React.js
- React Router
- Axios
- Tailwind CSS / Bootstrap (edit as needed)

### Backend (Node)
- Node.js
- Express
- MongoDB / PostgreSQL (mention your DB)
- Mongoose / Sequelize (as applicable)
- JSON Web Tokens (JWT)

---

## 🛠️ Installation

### Prerequisites
- Node.js and npm installed
- Git
- MongoDB/PostgreSQL (running locally or on cloud)
  
---

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Khowshikksharma/Eduflex.git
cd Eduflex
```
### 2. Set Project Backend
```bash
cd backend
npm install
# Create a .env file based on .env.example
npm start
```

### 3. Set Project Frontend
```bash
cd ../frontend
npm install
npm start
```

### 4. Make sure Environmental Variable setted
```bash
PORT=5000
MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_connection_string
JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret
```

### 5. Testing 
```bash
npm test
```

